API-06: reject a link whose start and end nodes are the same

EN_addlink did not check that its two end nodes differ, although
EN_setlinknodes and the input file parser reject a self-loop with error
222. The self-loop puts a junction in its own adjacency list, and
genmmd() then reads past a heap buffer when EN_openH orders the nodes.
EN_addlink now returns 222. This is the same check that upstream PR
#940 added after 83e25bb.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-06_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..2da8509 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -3425,6 +3425,9 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_addlink(EN_Project p, const char *id, int linkType,
     n2 = hashtable_find(net->NodeHashTable, toNode);
     if (n1 == 0 || n2 == 0) return 203;
 
+    // Check that nodes are not the same
+    if (n1 == n2) return 222;
+
     // Check that valve link has legal connections
     if (linkType > PUMP)
     {
